{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "lem:moving-offset-carter-geometry",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "statement": "Fix a rational compact polytope \\(C\\subset\\mathbb R^d\\).  Let \\(c_n,\\widehat c_n\\in\\mathcal K_0\\) lie eventually in one fixed compact set \\(C_c\\subset\\mathcal K_0\\), suppose \\(\\|\\widehat c_n-c_n\\|_\\infty\\le\\xi_n\\), and define\n\\[\n\\chi_n(C)=d_n(C)+\\delta_n(C)+\\xi_n,\n\\qquad\nA_0=\\sum_{j\\in\\mathcal J_0^{\\mathrm{act}}}\n\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}\\{a_j'\\Sigma_0a_j\\}^{1/2}}.\n\\]\nFor any supplied Gaussian rule in the \\(\\widehat c_n\\)-offset experiment and any supplied upper bound \\(\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\ge\\chi_n(C)\\), the parameter-independent Carter and score transfer has semantic coverage discrepancy and normalized separated-risk discrepancy on \\(C\\) at most\n\\[\n\\Delta_n(C)=C_{2/\\kappa}\\frac{|\\mathcal J|\\log|\\mathcal J|}{\\sqrt n}\n+\\operatorname{Err}_{\\Sigma,n}(C)\n+\\{H_C+2A_0\\}\\overline\\chi_n(C),\n\\qquad H_C=H(C,C_c).\n\\]\nThe upper bound \\(\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\) is arbitrary and need not be effective.  If \\(\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\to0\\), then \\(\\Delta_n(C)\\to0\\).  This conclusion constructs no Gaussian rule and invokes no effective-compatible-density premise.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "n",
      "u",
      "d",
      "pn",
