    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:multinomial-interior",
      "ass:multinomial-base-convergence",
      "ass:multinomial-local-expansion",
      "def:moving-slack-system",
      "def:multinomial-transfer-handle",
      "lem:compact-moving-remainder-covariance",
      "lem:finite-completed-arrangement-stability",
      "prop:carter-fixed-m-positive-cell",
      "lem:bounded-semantic-transfer-by-tv"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "\\textbf{Technique: exact affine-slack coupling, compact-offset finite-arrangement stability, and bounded Gaussian boundary density.}\n\nFor every active facet, \\(\\text{def:moving-slack-system}\\) gives the exact identity\n\\[\n\\zeta_{n,j}(u)-\\{\\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'u\\}\n=(c_{n,j}-\\widehat c_{n,j})+e_{n,j}(u).\n\\tag{15}\n\\]\nConsequently,\n\\[\n\\max_j\\sup_{u\\in C}\n\\left|\\zeta_{n,j}(u)-\\{\\widehat c_{n,j}+a_j'u\\}\\right|\n\\le\\delta_n(C)+\\xi_n\\le\\chi_n(C).\n\\tag{16}\n\\]\nThe hypothesis that \\(c_n\\) and \\(\\widehat c_n\\) lie in the same fixed compact \\(C_c\\subset\\mathcal K_0\\) is now used: it permits invocation of \\(\\text{lem:finite-completed-arrangement-stability}\\) with its single finite constant\n\\(H_C=H(C,C_c)\\).  Together with the centered score displacement \\(d_n(C)\\), (16) matches every completed semantic label mean and every separated-risk mean to the \\(\\widehat c_n\\)-offset arrangement at Mahalanobis displacement at most\n\\[\nH_C\\chi_n(C).\n\\tag{17}\n\\]\nThe lemma's directed Hausdorff part handles rival semantic unions, and its equality convention retains all incident labels.\n\nFor each active \\(j\\), positivity of \\(\\Sigma_0\\) and \\(a_j\\ne0\\) imply \\(a_j'\\Sigma_0a_j>0\\).  The same density calculation as in (12) gives, uniformly over the offset and the Gaussian mean,\n\\[\n\\Pr_h\\{|c_j+a_j'W_0|\\le s\\}\n\\le\\min\\left\\{1,\n\\frac{2s}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}\\{a_j'\\Sigma_0a_j\\}^{1/2}}\\right\\}.\n\\tag{18}\n\\]\nThus \\(\\mathfrak b_0(s)\\le A_0s\\).  In the moving-boundary comparison take the collar tolerance to be\n\\(\\tau_n=\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\).  Because\n\\(\\chi_n(C)\\le\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\), the strict failure indicator\n\\(\\mathbf1\\{\\chi_n(C)>\\tau_n\\}\\) equals zero, while\n\\[\n\\mathfrak b_0\\{\\tau_n+\\chi_n(C)\\}\n\\le\\mathfrak b_0\\{2\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\}\n\\le2A_0\\overline\\chi_n(C).\n\\tag{19}\n\\]\nAlso (17) is at most \\(H_C\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\).\n\nBy \\(\\text{prop:carter-fixed-m-positive-cell}\\), Carter's parameter-independent kernel contributes\n\\(C_{2/\\kappa}|\\mathcal J|\\log|\\mathcal J|/\\sqrt n\\) on \\(C\\).  The affine score-normal replacement contributes \\(\\operatorname{Err}_{\\Sigma,n}(C)\\), and \\(\\text{lem:bounded-semantic-transfer-by-tv}\\) applies both to coverage indicators and to \\(\\ell_0\\in[0,1]\\).  Adding these nonnegative charges to (17)--(19) proves\n\\[\n\\Delta_n(C)\n=C_{2/\\kappa}\\frac{|\\mathcal J|\\log|\\mathcal J|}{\\sqrt n}\n+\\operatorname{Err}_{\\Sigma,n}(C)\n+(H_C+2A_0)\\overline\\chi_n(C).\n\\tag{20}\n\\]\nIf \\(\\overline\\chi_n(C)\\to0\\), compactness of the fixed offset set keeps \\(H_C\\) fixed, \\(\\operatorname{Err}_{\\Sigma,n}(C)\\to0\\) by \\(\\text{lem:compact-moving-remainder-covariance}\\), and the Carter term vanishes.  Hence \\(\\Delta_n(C)\\to0\\).",
    "justification": "This lemma isolates the unconditional moving-offset statistical comparison from the unresolved construction of a finite Gaussian rule.",
    "gap": "Its upper bound may be qualitative unless rational envelopes for the centered expansion and covariance replacement are supplied.",
    "consumer": "The moving-offset theorem uses it with one compact set containing both the actual and rationalized offsets.",
